From 7e73fe2789fdb44467722921689cfe4f55676761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 276/280] WIP: clk: rockchip: rk3568: add PLL rates for the
 1000/1001 HDMI clocks

The HPLL rate table has the integer HDMI pixel clocks but none of their
1000/1001 variants. The PLL rounds a request down to the next table
rate, so 148.352 MHz becomes 135 MHz, and the dw-hdmi glue rejects the
mode because that is more than 0.1% away. Every 59.94, 29.97 and
23.976 Hz mode is removed.

Add fractional entries at the rates DRM uses for these modes: 593.407,
296.703, 148.352 and 74.176 MHz. Each runs the VCO of its integer
counterpart scaled by 1000/1001.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

